CYFR Licensing
==============

This project is dual-licensed. The default license is **Apache License
2.0**; files under `apps/cyfr/lib/sanctum/` (Sanctum — the auth, policy,
and tenancy layer) and the matching tests under `apps/cyfr/test/sanctum/`
are licensed under the **Functional Source License, Version 1.1,
Apache 2.0 Future License** (FSL-1.1-Apache-2.0). Everything else,
including the tenancy schema migrations, is Apache-2.0.

License determination is purely per-file via the `SPDX-License-Identifier`
header on line 1 of each source file (there is no `REUSE.toml`). The
canonical license texts live in the `LICENSES/` directory, and the FSL
zone — exactly the two Sanctum directories — is enforced mechanically by
`.github/workflows/license-lint.yml`.

* `LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt` — Apache License 2.0 (OSI-approved).
* `LICENSES/FSL-1.1-Apache-2.0.txt` — Functional Source License 1.1
  with Apache 2.0 as the future license (i.e., each file becomes
  Apache-2.0-licensed two years after its most recent commit).

In short: the FSL restricts third parties from offering CYFR as a
competing hosted or managed service. Internal use is unrestricted.
Two years after each commit, the affected files convert to Apache 2.0.

See `FAIR_SOURCE.md` (if present) and the `README.md` "License" section
for the practical implications for self-hosting, distributing, and
contributing.

Copyright 2026 CYFR Works Inc.
